    {
      "id": "f2022-final-q20",
      "number": 20,
      "points": 8,
      "stem": "Using the fact that $\\tan^{-1} x = \\sum_{k=0}^{\\infty} \\frac{(-1)^k}{2k + 1} x^{2k+1}$, $|x| \\le 1$, use the first two terms of the Maclaurin series for $3x^3 \\tan^{-1}(2x)$ to estimate\n\n$$\n\\int_0^1 3x^3 \\tan^{-1}(2x)\\, dx\n$$",
      "choices": [
        {
          "label": "A",
          "text": "$\\frac{37}{50}$"
