        {
          "label": "D",
          "text": "$\\frac{2}{35}$"
        },
        {
          "label": "E",
          "text": "$\\frac{3}{5}$"
        }
      ],
      "answer": "D",
      "lessonIds": [
        "L32"
      ],
      "sourcePage": 12,
      "solution": "**Note on this question:** The Maclaurin series for $\\tan^{-1}(2x)$ converges only for $|2x|\\le1$, that is $|x|\\le\\frac{1}{2}$, but the integral runs up to $x=1$, where two terms of the series are not a reliable estimate. Following the procedure the stem asks for gives $\\int_0^1(6x^4-8x^6)\\,dx=\\frac{6}{5}-\\frac{8}{7}=\\frac{2}{35}$, choice D, which is the stored answer; the true value of the integral is about $0.747$, close to choice A.",
